{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Jethro heard.</b> Jethro had seven names: Yeter, Hobab, Hever, Keni, Putiel, Reuel. And some say Reuel was Jethro's father, and what is written ״ותבאנה אל רעואל אביהם״ — it is the way of children, who call their father's father 'father.' And it is difficult for the one who says Reuel is Jethro: if he also holds that Hobab is Jethro, as Rashi explained — Hobab, because he loved (חיבב) the Torah — then if so, what does the verse mean ״ויאמר משה לחובב״? And one may answer that the one who says Hobab is Jethro — what does the verse teach by ״ותבאנה אל רעואל״? That children, etc. [call their grandfather 'father']. And two names were called to him: Yeter, because he added (יתר) one passage in the Torah; Hobab, because he loved (חיבב) the Torah. Even so it is difficult, for there are not seven names, as Rashi explained. And furthermore it is difficult, [for Rashi] himself contradicts himself, for he wrote that seven names were called to him. And furthermore, for the one who says Reuel is Jethro, it must be that Hobab is not Jethro. And furthermore, it is written that Hobab is Jethro, as it is written ״ומבני חובב חותן משה״. And furthermore it is difficult: how can one say that he was called both Hobab and Keni, when it is written ״וחבר הקני״ — separate from ״קין״ etc. — if so, this implies that Hever the Keni is the son of Jethro, Moses' father-in-law. And this requires investigation."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The last difficulty appears to read Judges 4:11 (וחבר הקני) as distinguishing 'Hever the Keni' as a separate person from Jethro; the citation וגו' after קין is unclear — the verse reads נפרד מקין, meaning 'separated from Cain,' but the compiler seems to parse it differently."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:28.654342830Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}